<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manikya Lal Varma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1897">1897</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Manikya Lal Verma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manikya Lal Varma was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> activist from Mewar and a leader of the praja mandal movement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a>. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mewar-praja-mandal">Mewar Praja Mandal</a> in 1938 and, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> joined the union in April 1948, became prime minister of the United State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, heading its first popular government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manikya-lal-varma.jpg" alt="Manikya Lal Varma" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shalivahan2 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manikya_Lal_Verma.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
